---
/**
 * The booking and cancellation policy.
 *
 * The playbook calls the cancellation window the top pre-booking objection in
 * the segment and says it is almost never answered (playbook-sim-venue.md §4).
 * It is REQUIRED on /book and it is required here.
 *
 * It IS published, and now so is ours. The 48-hour rule is quoted verbatim from
 * the venue's own /booking and /bookingstillwater pages and mirrored word for
 * word on /book.
 *
 * ⚠️ This page previously withheld it, on the reasoning that shipping an
 * unconfirmed cancellation charge could cost a customer money. That instinct is
 * right and worth keeping — but it was applied to a fact we already had, and the
 * result told visitors the venue had not supplied something they publish in two
 * places. Withhold what is genuinely unknown; do not withhold what is merely
 * unverified when the source is the client's own site.
 *
 * ⚠️ Note: seo-map.md §4 redirects the old /policy to /policies. This build ships
 * /policy as the canonical booking-policy URL; reconcile the redirect map before
 * launch so the two do not both resolve.
 *
 * VOICE PASS 2026-08-04 (FW-4001). One of the four flattest pages, and the one
 * where the brief needs the most care: warmth on a page of binding terms has to
 * come from PLAIN SPEECH, never from making light of the terms themselves. So
 * the register lifts in the framing — why the page exists, what a rule is
 * actually for, the quiet-days line — and stops dead at the waiver, which is
 * reproduced straight. Not one rule, window, charge or clause moved.
 *
 * ── STUB PASS 2026-08-05 (FW-4013) ─────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Three raw `STUB —` blocks rendered here in production. They are not all the
 * same kind of thing, and the point of this ticket is that they were treated as
 * though they were:
 *
 *   Paying          a note that our description is transcribed and unverified.
 *                   That is a message to the READER standing next to a fact, so
 *                   it becomes a `PendingTag` — which renders in production by
 *                   design. The surcharge question behind it is ours: `StubNote`.
 *
 *   The waiver      the note says a Stillwater customer is agreeing to a waiver
 *                   that names only Lakeville. That is material to the person
 *                   reading it, so it stays visible, rewritten as an address to
 *                   them. The entity-name reconciliation is ours: `StubNote`.
 *
 *   Still to be     four rules a customer would look for and not find. Those are
 *   written         gaps, not tasks, so they take the gap system's first mark —
 *                   `GapCell` *Not yet set*, customer-facing on purpose.
 *
 * Nothing here is invented to fill a gap. An unknown rule stays unknown and
 * marked, which is the whole point of having a mark for it.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import PendingTag from '../components/venue/PendingTag.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import { getVenues, telHref } from '../lib/venues';

const venues = await getVenues();

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Booking & Cancellation Policy — The Links, MN',
  metaDescription:
    'How booking, payment and cancellation work at The Links in Lakeville and Stillwater, Minnesota. Read this before you reserve a simulator bay.',
};

/**
 * House rules, supplied by the owner 2026-09-11. These replaced three `GapCell`
 * marks — the page could not answer them before, and said so rather than
 * guessing, which is why the answers read as rules and not as hedges.
 *
 * Dress keeps the owner's order deliberately: what is encouraged first, what is
 * forbidden second. "Golf attire recommended, street shoes prohibited" is a
 * welcome with one hard edge; led with the prohibition it is a dress code, and
 * this is a venue whose whole argument is that you do not need to be a golfer.
 */
const houseRules = [
  [
    'Bringing your own food or drink',
    'Outside food and drink are not allowed at either venue. Both have their own menu and bar, and the kitchen is part of what you are booking.',
  ],
  [
    'Dress and footwear',
    'Golf attire is recommended but not required — come comfortable. The one rule is footwear: street shoes are not allowed on the playing surfaces, so wear golf shoes or trainers you can play in.',
  ],
  [
    'Group and event deposits',
    'Deposit and cancellation terms for a private event depend on the date and the size of the group. Contact the venue and they will go through it with you.',
  ],
  [
    'Items left behind',
    'Anything left at either venue goes into lost and found and is kept for seven days. After that it is donated or thrown away. Neither venue is responsible for items left in its facilities, so check the bay before you go.',
  ],
];

/** The rules the current site does publish, in plain words. */
const rules = [
  [
    'You pay for the whole booking',
    'You are responsible for the full time you reserved, even if you finish early. Book the hours you want, not the hours you might want.',
  ],
  [
    'Your slot ends five minutes early',
    'Every booking finishes at five minutes to the hour so the next group can start on time. Plan the last hole accordingly.',
  ],
  [
    'We may move you to a different bay',
    'We reserve the right to move a booking to another bay to fit the tee sheet together.',
  ],
  [
    'How long to book for',
    'Roughly one hour per person for 18 holes. One person is about an hour, four people in one bay is about four. If that is longer than you want, book two bays or play nine.',
  ],
  /* Was a `notSet` gap in "Rules we have not set yet" below until CJ supplied the
     policy on 2026-09-03. Worded to match /book — keep the two in step. */
  [
    'Walk-ins',
    'Walk-ins are welcome, but not guaranteed to have a spot. Reserve a bay if you would rather not risk the drive, or ring ahead and ask what is free.',
  ],
];

/**
 * THE LIABILITY WAIVER — restored 2026-08-04 (FW-4000) from
 * `_ingest/raw/policy.html`, which is the client's own live page.
 *
 * ⚠️ This is the part of the restore that mattered most, and the reason the
 * ticket said to read the waiver language specifically. Their policy page runs
 * 1768 words and ours ran 625; almost the whole difference was this. We had
 * quietly dropped a binding document — not a marketing paragraph — and replaced
 * it with a stub that said a waiver "is needed", on a site whose booking flow
 * tells the customer they have already agreed to one.
 *
 * It is reproduced faithfully, not paraphrased and not summarised. The headings
 * and the clause order are theirs. Where a clause is rendered as plain English
 * rather than legalese it is marked as a plain-English summary and the operative
 * wording is kept alongside it, because a shortened waiver is a changed waiver.
 *
 * ⚠️ THE COMPANY DEFINITION WAS CHANGED BY THE OWNER, 2026-09-11, and that is
 * why it no longer matches the waiver as the old site published it. It now
 * names both entities — UDBA 10 LLC dba The Links of Lakeville and URN 8 LLC
 * dba The Links of Stillwater — retiring "Head Honchos, LLC dba Lakeville
 * Links", which was one of two conflicting Lakeville names in circulation.
 *
 * It was asked for as "UDBA 10 … dba The Links of Stillwater & URN 8 … dba The
 * Links of Stillwater", naming Stillwater twice and no Lakeville entity at all.
 * That was put back to the owner rather than published, because the old site's
 * own membership terms say UDBA 10 trades as Lakeville, and the owner confirmed
 * that reading. A liability waiver is the last place to resolve a typo by
 * guessing.
 *
 * ⚠️ THE DOCUMENT IS NOW INTERNALLY INCONSISTENT, AND DELIBERATELY SO. Company
 * names two venues; the FACILITY clause still gives the Lakeville address only.
 * That was not part of the instruction and is not ours to take: widening which
 * building a waiver covers is a legal act, not a copy edit. It is stated to the
 * reader and flagged for the lawyer instead of quietly reconciled.
 */
const waiverDefinitions: [string, string][] = [
  ['Company', 'UDBA 10 LLC dba The Links of Lakeville & URN 8 LLC dba The Links of Stillwater.'],
  [
    'Equipment',
    'Golf equipment including but not limited to golf clubs, golf balls, tees, gloves and footwear, as well as electronic golf simulators and all of their ancillary equipment.',
  ],
  [
    'Facility',
    "The Company's facilities located at 17630 Juniper Path, Suite H, Lakeville, MN 55044 & 5862 Omaha Ave N, Stillwater, MN 55082.",
  ],
  ['Golfing', 'Use of the Facility and/or Equipment.'],
];

/** What you confirm about yourself. Their clause order. */
const waiverAcknowledgements = [
  'You are solely responsible for your own health and safety.',
  'You are physically capable of golfing and using the equipment.',
  'You have no pre-existing physical or medical condition that would put you or anyone else at risk while golfing or using the equipment.',
  'You are at least 18 years of age.',
  'You will tell staff immediately if you notice damaged equipment, and you will not use it — damaged equipment raises every one of the risks above.',
];

/** The safety rules, verbatim in substance. These are the ones staff enforce. */
const safetyRules = [
  'Before you swing, check that nobody is close enough to be hit by the club.',
  'Pay attention to what is going on around you.',
  'Only swing inside the designated area of the bay, and only to hit into the simulator.',
  'Do not swing until everyone is behind the caution line or behind the tables at each bay.',
  'Watch your step. The hitting platform moves during play, and a moving floor is a trip hazard.',
  'Stay behind the caution line while somebody else is hitting.',
  'No food or drink past the caution line.',
  'Keep your drinking to a level that does not make you a risk to yourself or anyone else.',
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata} subscribe={false}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-prose-page px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold lg:text-5xl">Booking &amp; cancellation policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-inkMuted">
      Everything you are agreeing to when you reserve a bay at The Links of Lakeville or The Links of Stillwater. All of
      it is on this page, in front of you, rather than behind a checkbox at the end of the booking. Booking itself
      happens in Whoosh, our reservation system.
    </p>

    {
      /* The cancellation window goes FIRST because it is the question people came
         for — the segment's top pre-booking objection, and almost nobody answers it.

         This section previously said the policy "is not confirmed and must not be
         guessed." That was wrong: the venue publishes it, verbatim, on /booking and
         /bookingstillwater. Withholding it was the right instinct applied to a fact we
         actually had — and it read as though the client had failed to supply something
         they had in fact published. Source: _ingest/raw/booking.html. */
    }
    <section class="mt-10 border-l-slab border-primary bg-surface p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Cancellations</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg">
        <strong>Cancel at least 48 hours before your reservation and it is free.</strong> Inside 48 hours you may be charged
        for the full bay reservation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        You cancel the same way you booked — in Whoosh, the reservation system. At Stillwater, cancel through the Whoosh
        app.
      </p>
      {
        /* All three of these were listed as genuinely unpublished until
          2026-08-04 (client-answers.md §5). Note the deliberate vagueness on
          moving a booking: the venue does NOT want a stated deadline, so do not
          invent one — "as soon as you can" is the policy, not a placeholder. */
      }
      <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Moving a booking</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        You can move one. Tell us as soon as you know — the earlier you do, the easier it is to find you another slot.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">If you do not turn up</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        A no-show is charged for the full bay. The bay was held for you and nobody else could book it, which is the
        whole reason the 48-hour window exists.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">If we have to close</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        We reserve the right to close — weather, a burst pipe, the sort of thing nobody plans. But we will not close on
        a day with bookings on it without contacting you first.
      </p>
      {
        /* The operational-honesty line, restored verbatim from the client's own
          homepage (`_ingest/raw/home.html`, FW-4000). It sits under their
          published hours there, and it is repeated on the hours tables here. It
          is the sort of candour the rest of the site is built on, and it is
          genuinely useful: it is the difference between a wasted drive and a
          booked bay. */
      }
      <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Quiet days</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        In the venue's own words: <strong
          >if there are no pre-booked bay times, we reserve the right to open late or close early.</strong
        > Nobody is sitting in an empty building at 11am on a Tuesday on the off chance. Book the bay and the door is open
        when you get there — that is the whole trick.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Paying</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        A card is required to make a reservation at either venue, and the two venues handle it differently:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-inkMuted">
        <li>
          <strong>Lakeville</strong> — a hold is placed on your card. The charge transfers to the till at the venue, so you
          can split the bill with your group at the end.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stillwater</strong> — your card is charged in full at the time of booking.
        </li>
      </ul>
      {
        /* The pending mark on these two payment rules came off on 2026-09-11:
          the owner confirmed them, which is what it was waiting for. They were
          transcribed from booking pages this rebuild deletes, so until then they
          were believed rather than verified, and `PendingTag` said so in
          production because that caveat was addressed to the reader standing
          next to the fact rather than to us.

          The surcharge question below is a different one and is still open. */
      }
      <StubNote
        class="mt-4"
        needs="Confirm the 3% credit-card surcharge that appears on the Lakeville menu, and whether it applies to bay time as well as food. The two payment rules above are confirmed as of 2026-09-11."
      />
    </section>

    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Your booking</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 space-y-6">
        {
          rules.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    {
      /* THE WAIVER. Restored in full — see the note on `waiverDefinitions` for
        why this is the most important part of the page and what is wrong with
        it that is not ours to fix. */
    }
    <section class="mt-section" id="waiver">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">The liability waiver</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        When you submit a reservation you confirm your details are correct and you agree to the booking terms above
        <em>and</em> to the liability waiver below. It is here so you can read it before you book rather than discover it
        in a checkbox. It is long because waivers are long; the short version is that golf clubs move fast, the floor under
        you moves too, and you are agreeing to be careful.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 border-l-slab border-ink/25 pl-6">
        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold">Definitions</h3>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3">
          {
            waiverDefinitions.map(([term, meaning]) => (
              <div>
                <dt class="font-semibold">&ldquo;{term}&rdquo;</dt>
                <dd class="text-inkMuted">{meaning}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Acknowledgement and assumption of risk</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          By coming to the facility, using the equipment, being around the equipment, or golfing, you accept that it
          carries risks, hazards and dangers. Those include, but are not limited to: equipment malfunction, or defective
          or negligent design or manufacture of equipment; careless or negligent instruction or supervision; slips,
          falls, accidents and collisions; the negligence of other people; and being hit by a club, a ball, equipment or
          any other object that comes loose — any of which may injure you or your property, or a minor with you or
          theirs. You knowingly and freely accept and assume all of them.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">You also confirm that:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-inkMuted">
          {waiverAcknowledgements.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Release of liability</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          In return for being allowed into the facility to watch or to play, you — on behalf of yourself, your personal
          representatives, heirs, successors, assigns, guardians and legal representatives — fully and forever release,
          waive, discharge, hold harmless, defend and indemnify the Company and its affiliates, contractors, agents,
          employees, officers, directors and shareholders (the &ldquo;Releasees&rdquo;) from any and all claims,
          demands, suits, actions, causes of action or liability of any kind, for any damages, losses, injuries, death,
          costs or expenses (including legal fees and disbursements) arising out of or relating to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-inkMuted">
          <li>your attendance at the facility;</li>
          <li>your golfing and/or use of the equipment;</li>
          <li>
            anything done by a third party, including other people at the facility, golfing, or using the equipment; and
          </li>
          <li>
            any negligent or intentional acts, whether directly or indirectly connected to the facility, golfing or the
            equipment.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          For the avoidance of doubt, you agree to hold harmless and indemnify the Company and the Releasees from all
          liability for any damage whatsoever, including loss of property or personal injury, resulting from your
          attendance, your golfing, or your use of the equipment.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Safety rules</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          You agree to follow the Company's safety rules at all times. They include, but are not limited to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-inkMuted">{safetyRules.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}</ul>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">General provisions</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          You acknowledge that the Releasees rely on this waiver in letting you in, and that without it you would not be
          allowed to attend, golf, or use the equipment.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          You acknowledge that while you are at the facility the Company or its agents may take photographs, video or
          other recordings of you or any minor with you, and may use them — along with your name and likeness, and that
          of any minor — in advertising, promotional material and any other media.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          This waiver is the entire agreement between the parties on this subject and supersedes all other agreements,
          oral or written. Except as provided here, it may not be amended or modified except in writing signed by both
          parties. Headings and numbering are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation, and words like
          &ldquo;hereof&rdquo;, &ldquo;herein&rdquo; and &ldquo;hereunder&rdquo; relate to the whole waiver rather than
          to the clause they sit in.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          If any term is found invalid or unenforceable, the rest still stands and applies separately, and the
          unenforceable term is treated as amended only as far as needed to make it enforceable while keeping the
          parties' intent. This waiver is governed by the laws of the State of Minnesota and the applicable laws of the
          United States, and each party irrevocably submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Minnesota courts. Any
          reference to gender includes all genders, and the singular includes the plural and vice versa.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">If you bring anyone under 18</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
          You represent that you are the parent, legal guardian or authorised custodian of any person under 18 (the
          &ldquo;Minor&rdquo;) who comes in with you or whom you bring in, and that you have the legal authority to sign
          this waiver on their behalf. You agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Company and the Releasees against
          any claim the Minor has now or may have in future arising out of their attendance, golfing or use of the
          equipment. If you do not in fact have that authority, you agree to indemnify the Company and the Releasees
          against any and all claims made by the Minor or their legal representatives.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">You also confirm that:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-inkMuted">
          <li>the Minor is physically capable of golfing and using the equipment;</li>
          <li>
            the Minor has no pre-existing physical or medical condition that would put them or anyone else at risk while
            golfing, using the equipment or being in the facility;
          </li>
          <li>the Minor will be supervised by you throughout their stay; and</li>
          <li>the Company is not responsible for loss of the Minor's property while they are at the facility.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-8 border-y-score border-ink py-4 font-semibold">
          I HAVE READ THIS LIABILITY WAIVER, I FULLY UNDERSTAND ITS TERMS, I UNDERSTAND THAT I AM GIVING UP RIGHTS BY
          ENTERING INTO THIS LIABILITY WAIVER INCLUDING WAIVING CERTAIN LEGAL RIGHTS WHICH I OR MY HEIRS, NEXT OF KIN,
          EXECUTORS, ADMINISTRATORS, ASSIGNS AND REPRESENTATIVES MAY HAVE AGAINST THE COMPANY AND THE RELEASEES AND I DO
          SO FREELY AND VOLUNTARILY WITHOUT ANY INDUCEMENT.
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        /* Production-visible, and it has to be. A Stillwater customer is being
          shown a waiver that names only Lakeville; that is material to the
          person reading it, not a note to ourselves. So it is rewritten as an
          address to them — plain, no build language — and the entity
          reconciliation, which really is ours, moves to the `StubNote` below. */
      }
      <p class="mt-6 border-l-slab border-ink/25 bg-surface p-6 text-inkBody">
        <strong>Which venue this waiver names.</strong> Both of them. The Company is UDBA 10 LLC dba The Links of Lakeville
        and URN 8 LLC dba The Links of Stillwater, and the facility is defined as both addresses — Juniper Path in Lakeville
        and Omaha Avenue North in Stillwater. Whichever venue you booked, this is the waiver that applies to you. It has not
        been through a lawyer yet, which is said plainly at the top of this page and is worth knowing before you rely on any
        of it.
      </p>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-4"
        needs="For a lawyer, not a copywriter. RESOLVED 2026-09-11: both halves of the waiver now cover both venues. The owner confirmed UDBA 10 LLC dba The Links of Lakeville — retiring 'Head Honchos, LLC dba Lakeville Links', one of two conflicting Lakeville names — alongside URN 8 LLC dba The Links of Stillwater, confirmed 2026-09-02, and gave the Stillwater address for the Facility clause. STILL OPEN, and it is the whole of what is left: none of this document has been through a lawyer. A waiver assembled from a client's answers is not a reviewed waiver. See FW-4008."
      />
    </section>

    {
      /* ⚠️ THIS WAS "RULES WE HAVE NOT SET YET" AND IS NOT ANY MORE. All three
        gaps — outside food and drink, dress and footwear, event deposits — were
        answered by the owner on 2026-09-11, so they become plain rules and the
        `GapCell` grid goes with them. "Items left" is new in the same pass.

        Worth keeping in mind if a rule is ever withdrawn: the gap system exists
        so an unanswered question is VISIBLY unanswered rather than silently
        absent. Deleting a rule from this list does not restore that — put the
        `GapCell` back. */
    }
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">House rules</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose-page text-inkMuted">The things people ask about most often before they arrive.</p>
      <dl class="mt-6 space-y-6">
        {
          houseRules.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 max-w-prose-page text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-6"
        needs="The three gaps that stood here — outside food and drink, dress and footwear, group and event deposits — were answered by the owner on 2026-09-11 and are now plain rules, alongside a new one on items left behind. What is still open on this page: the 3% credit-card surcharge under Paying, and the facility clause of the waiver has never been through a lawyer."
      />
    </section>

    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Ask us instead</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">
        If something here is not answered, phone the venue — it is faster than email and someone is there during opening
        hours.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1 text-inkMuted">
        {
          venues.map((venue) => (
            <li class="mt-s3">
              {venue.data.name}:{' '}
              <a href={telHref(venue.data.phone)} class="font-semibold underline">
                {venue.data.phone}
              </a>
              {venue.data.phoneNote && <PendingTag class="mt-s2" reason={venue.data.phoneNote} />}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
    <section class="mt-section rounded bg-surface p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Ready to book</h2>
      <div class="mt-6"><BookButton size="lg" /></div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
